// Welcome, humans!
 This is an empty writing archive you can copy for anyone. It includes the shared
 layout, search, sorting, keyboard navigation, and HTML/plain-text exports.

// Create a person's folder
 From the parent bu directory:
  python3 bunew/scripts/new_person.py bubill "Bill Gates" https://www.gatesnotes.com/
  cd bubill
  npm install
  npm run build
  npm run check
  npm run serve
 Open http://localhost:8000. Existing folders are never overwritten.
 Or copy bunew manually and edit site.json and the package name in package.json.
 site.json sets the site name, author, original URL, and optional published baseUrl.
 Builds regenerate head.scroll, search.scroll, and the page below these comments.
 These opening comments are preserved; page template changes go in scripts/configure.py.

// Port someone's writing
 Save original pages in originals/ and images in assets/.
 Convert each article body to originals/<slug>.scroll using native Scroll paragraphs,
 headings, lists, and links. Leave out page metadata and header/footer includes.
 Use assets/image.jpg for local images. Fetching and conversion depend on the source
 website; scripts/import_blog.py accepts Scroll bodies, not arbitrary web pages.
 Add each article to archive.json:
  [
    {"slug": "article-slug", "title": "Article title", "date": "2026-01-01", "url": "https://example.com/article-slug"}
  ]
 Run npm run import, npm run build, then npm run check.
 Reimporting replaces matching post sources. To remove a post, remove its manifest
 entry and its .scroll, .html, and .txt files before rebuilding.
 You can also write top-level <slug>.scroll files directly: title, date, canonicalUrl,
 then post-header.scroll, the body, and footer.scroll. Keep archive.json aligned.

// Style and publish
 bu.scroll is the shared layout; blog.parsers supplies archive and source links.
 Run the parent's ./update.sh to sync bu.scroll into all person folders, then rebuild.
 style.css and site.js are generated from style.scroll and site.scroll.
 Upload the built folder to a static host. .nojekyll supports GitHub Pages; add CNAME
 only when you choose a domain. Nothing deploys automatically.
 Clone URLs follow https://github.com/breck7/<site name>; adjust bu.scroll if needed.

// John Collison source import
 Imported for http://johncollison.ie/ on 2026-10-04. The domain is now parked and
 no longer resolves (DNS SERVFAIL), so every page was read from the Wayback Machine.
 22 posts: 20 from the WordPress blog at johncollison.ie/blog (2007-2008) and 2 from
 the Svbtle blog at blog.johncollison.ie (2012). The personal homepage and the
 /willitbeclear tool are not writing posts and are not included.
 None of the 9 article images were preserved by the Wayback Machine (they resolve to
 404), so each is shown as an "[Image not archived]" placeholder. Saved source HTML is
 in originals/html/ and the image accounting is in originals/images.json.
 Refresh with bs4, html5lib, and curl installed:
  python3 scripts/fetch_source.py
  python3 scripts/convert_source.py
  python3 scripts/fetch_images.py
  npm run import
  npm run build
  npm run check
  python3 scripts/verify_source.py
 The GitHub repository breck7/bujohnnyc already existed; no deployment was performed.

title bujohnnyc — Archive
description boo John Collison. made by @breckyunits
permalink index.html
canonicalUrl http://johncollison.ie/
buildHtml
head.scroll

container 1120px
 id main
 role main
 addClass archive

# All posts
 id archive-heading

BU_ARCHIVE
clearStack
homeFooter.scroll
site.js
